 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 People clear debris after an air attack in Kyiv yesterday. Photo: Oleksii Filippov/AFP via Getty Images 🇺🇦 Secretary of State Marco Rubio told Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky in a phone call today that President Trump hasn't issued any kind of order to harm Ukraine. The call was an effort to push back on Ukrainian accusations that Trump is trying to coerce Zelensky into making concessions to Russia. More from Barak Ravid . 👨‍💼 Axios exclusive: Joel Kaplan, Meta's chief global affairs officer, will leave Meta next year after 15+ years as Mark Zuckerberg's top Washington adviser. Zuckerberg tells Axios: "Joel has worked on virtually every tough issue Meta has faced for more than 15 years." Go deeper . 💰 Thieves stole nearly $1 million worth of trading cards last week from a FedEx truck parked for 60-90 minutes outside a Professional Sports Authenticator grading center in Santa Ana, Calif., The Athletic reports. PSA had "graded" the cards for the owners, verifying authenticity and condition. High grades boost cards' resale value. Gift link . 
 
