 4. 🏀 1 sports thing: NBA tips off 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Cover : Mark Ulriksen for The New Yorker " Make It Two ," by artist Mark Ulriksen, is the cover of this week's issue of The New Yorker. The painting shows the joyous starting lineup of the New York Knicks, last season's champions .

 The 2026-27 NBA season tipped off this afternoon, with the Boston Celtics visiting the Detroit Pistons starting at 3 p.m. ET.

 ESPN's ball-knowers favor the Oklahoma City Thunder and San Antonio Spurs. 🏆 Knicks fans, still riding high on last year's historic championship run, are hoping for a repeat. That hasn't happened since the Golden State Warriors did it in 2017 and 2018. 

